The market is very crowded.
I walk a little further.
Nearby there is a small flower stall.
There are many marigold flowers there.
The fragrance of the flowers is very good.
An aunty is sitting at the stall.
She is making garlands of fresh flowers.
I stop there.
I look at the beautiful garlands.
Aunty looks at me.
She smiles warmly.
I do not ask her the price.
She tells me the price herself.
Aunty says, "Madam, one garland is for twenty rupees."
I want a garland for my door.
I say, "Aunty, please give me one garland."
I take twenty rupees out of my bag.
I give her the money.
She gives me a fresh marigold garland.
I say thank you to her.
